    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32220" root="غلث" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَلَثٌ</span></b>  <i>What is mixed:</i> as <i>wheat mixed with
barley.</i> (Msb.) [In the present day, it is used
as signifying <i>What is mixed with wheat</i> &amp;c., <i>of
those things that are taken forth and thrown
away;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَثٌ</span>. See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَلِيثٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [And its
pl.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغْلَاثٌ</span> is mentioned by Aboo-Ziyád El-Kilá-
bee as a term applied to <i>Several sorts of plants,</i>
(O, TA,) <i>not</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَقْل</span> <i>nor</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَمْض</span> <i>nor</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِضَاه</span>, (O,)
<i>among which are the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِكْرِش</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَلْفَآء</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَاج</span>
<i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَنْبُوت</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَصَف</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِشْرِق</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَنَا</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسَل</span>
<i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْدِىّ</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنْظَل</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنُّوم</span> <i>and</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِرْوَع</span> (O,
TA) &amp;c. (O.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَثٌ</span>.]

